WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.944 --> 00:00:12.415
&gt;&gt;&gt; In just a matter days, two

00:00:12.548 --> 00:00:14.583
women were injured in bison

00:00:14.717 --> 00:00:16.685
attacks while visiting national

00:00:16.819 --> 00:00:16.986
parks.

00:00:17.119 --> 00:00:18.754
Saturday in North Dakota a woman

00:00:18.888 --> 00:00:21.123
suffered injuries to her stomach

00:00:21.257 --> 00:00:22.792
and when bison charged her.

00:00:22.925 --> 00:00:26.228
On Monday, a bison gored a woman

00:00:26.228 --> 00:00:26.462
in Wyoming.

00:00:26.595 --> 00:00:27.263
Both were September to hospitals

00:00:27.396 --> 00:00:29.165
to be treated for their injuries

00:00:29.298 --> 00:00:30.666
and investigations into the

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:32.301
attacks are ongoing.

00:00:32.435 --> 00:00:34.270
Joining us now with more insight

00:00:34.403 --> 00:00:36.238
into this is yellowstone

00:00:36.238 --> 00:00:38.574
wildlife safari guide grant

00:00:38.707 --> 00:00:40.276
trchlt Johnson.

00:00:40.409 --> 00:00:40.709
Grant, wow.

00:00:40.843 --> 00:00:42.278
This sounds really scary and

00:00:42.411 --> 00:00:45.381
both of these incidents are

00:00:45.514 --> 00:00:46.615
different, but I wonder, are

00:00:46.749 --> 00:00:47.917
people just getting too close to

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:48.617
these animals or is something

00:00:48.751 --> 00:00:53.722
else happening here?

00:00:53.856 --> 00:00:55.191
&gt;&gt; So, overwhelmingly, the

00:00:55.324 --> 00:00:56.492
incidences between bison and

00:00:56.625 --> 00:00:58.260
people are a result of people

00:00:58.260 --> 00:00:59.395
getting too close to the

00:00:59.528 --> 00:00:59.728
animals.

00:00:59.862 --> 00:01:02.364
Right now we have a bit of a

00:01:02.498 --> 00:01:04.500
convergence of who factors.

00:01:04.633 --> 00:01:05.734
First, the beginning of the

00:01:05.868 --> 00:01:08.337
bison rut, the mating season.

00:01:08.471 --> 00:01:10.339
So both the male and female

00:01:10.473 --> 00:01:12.341
bison have elevated levels of

00:01:12.475 --> 00:01:13.609
hormones and that makes them a

00:01:13.742 --> 00:01:15.111
little bit more agitated, a

00:01:15.244 --> 00:01:16.345
little bit more competitive on

00:01:16.479 --> 00:01:18.280
the landscape.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:19.615
Secondly, July is the busiest

00:01:19.748 --> 00:01:22.318
month for people to be visiting

00:01:22.451 --> 00:01:22.885
the national parks.

00:01:23.018 --> 00:01:24.620
So the risk of being attacked by

00:01:24.753 --> 00:01:28.491
a bison or any other animal is

00:01:28.624 --> 00:01:29.692
outrageously low.

00:01:29.825 --> 00:01:31.527
With this many people in the

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:34.930
park, it's not surprising this

00:01:35.064 --> 00:01:35.564
time of year these things

00:01:35.698 --> 00:01:35.898
happen.

00:01:36.298 --> 00:01:37.566
&gt;&gt; I am going to ask the thing I

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:39.902
think everybody is thinking.

00:01:40.302 --> 00:01:40.803
It shouldn't be that hard to not

00:01:40.936 --> 00:01:41.971
go close to bison.

00:01:42.304 --> 00:01:44.974
Seems like a logical thing.

00:01:45.107 --> 00:01:46.308
So my initial question as I have

00:01:46.408 --> 00:01:47.143
seen these reports, is this a

00:01:47.276 --> 00:01:48.377
social media thing?

00:01:48.511 --> 00:01:50.479
Is this people trying to take

00:01:50.613 --> 00:01:50.946
pictures?

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:53.582
Why are people going so close

00:01:53.716 --> 00:01:54.617
based on your experience?

00:01:54.750 --> 00:01:57.987
&gt;&gt; So I think it's a bit of a

00:01:58.320 --> 00:01:59.388
few factors.

00:01:59.522 --> 00:02:00.656
I think for sure social media

00:02:00.789 --> 00:02:02.925
has been a negative influence.

00:02:03.058 --> 00:02:03.626
People are re-creating photos

00:02:03.759 --> 00:02:06.328
they have seen or a new one that

00:02:06.328 --> 00:02:08.364
no one has seen and doing risky

00:02:08.497 --> 00:02:11.333
behaviors is a way to get that

00:02:11.467 --> 00:02:11.967
done.

00:02:12.334 --> 00:02:13.702
Also, a lot of people don't have

00:02:13.836 --> 00:02:16.372
familiarity with real authentic

00:02:16.505 --> 00:02:16.739
wildlife.

00:02:16.872 --> 00:02:17.473
When they come to the areas they

00:02:17.606 --> 00:02:18.841
think they are visiting a zoo.

00:02:18.974 --> 00:02:20.342
And this is not a zoo.

00:02:20.342 --> 00:02:22.344
These are national parks, true

00:02:22.344 --> 00:02:25.014
wild, authentic wildernesses and

00:02:25.147 --> 00:02:26.348
these answers are wild and

00:02:26.348 --> 00:02:27.416
potentially dangerous if we push

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:28.350
the limits with them.

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:30.352
&gt;&gt; What is your advice to people

00:02:30.352 --> 00:02:32.788
if they find themselves -- we

00:02:32.922 --> 00:02:33.722
are looking at some scary

00:02:33.856 --> 00:02:35.157
footage there -- of a bison

00:02:35.291 --> 00:02:36.025
charging at one?

00:02:36.358 --> 00:02:38.494
What happens if you are in that

00:02:38.627 --> 00:02:38.861
situation?

00:02:38.994 --> 00:02:41.130
What would you advise people to

00:02:41.263 --> 00:02:42.531
do to basically save themselves

00:02:42.665 --> 00:02:43.566
from being seriously injured or

00:02:43.699 --> 00:02:46.902
perhaps even killed?

00:02:47.036 --> 00:02:48.470
&gt;&gt; So the park service is very

00:02:48.604 --> 00:02:49.972
clear on their rules that they

00:02:50.372 --> 00:02:51.040
have set forth.

00:02:51.173 --> 00:02:54.510
They are not just polite

00:02:54.643 --> 00:02:54.910
suggestions.

00:02:55.044 --> 00:02:55.644
This is the law in the national

00:02:55.778 --> 00:02:55.945
parks.

00:02:56.378 --> 00:02:58.414
If you are in your car, there is

00:02:58.547 --> 00:02:58.747
no risk.

00:02:58.881 --> 00:02:59.915
As long as you are pulled off

00:03:00.049 --> 00:03:03.085
the side of the road, stop, ento

00:03:03.219 --> 00:03:04.420
joy the wildlife, take photos.

00:03:04.553 --> 00:03:05.688
If you are outside of your car,

00:03:05.821 --> 00:03:07.223
walking, hiking or just standing

00:03:07.356 --> 00:03:08.824
on the side of the road, you

00:03:08.958 --> 00:03:11.227
need to stay certain safety

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:12.928
distances away from the animals.

00:03:13.062 --> 00:03:14.863
Bears and wolves, that's 100

00:03:14.997 --> 00:03:16.532
yards and all of the other

00:03:16.665 --> 00:03:19.602
animals, including bison, is 25

00:03:19.735 --> 00:03:19.902
yards.

00:03:20.035 --> 00:03:22.404
If you see the animal

00:03:22.404 --> 00:03:23.272
drastically changing behavior

00:03:23.405 --> 00:03:24.974
because of your presence you are

00:03:25.107 --> 00:03:26.642
too close, even if you are

00:03:26.775 --> 00:03:27.276
beyond those limits.

00:03:27.409 --> 00:03:29.478
With bison, they are nice enough

00:03:29.612 --> 00:03:32.414
to give us warning signs they

00:03:32.481 --> 00:03:33.415
are getting agitated.

00:03:33.549 --> 00:03:35.884
You will see an exaggerated head

00:03:36.018 --> 00:03:36.986
bobbing, scratching and stomping

00:03:37.119 --> 00:03:38.053
at the ground.

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:40.422
And you will see their tail go

00:03:40.422 --> 00:03:40.556
up.

00:03:40.556 --> 00:03:42.424
If you see any of those factors

00:03:42.491 --> 00:03:44.827
happening, back up, increase the

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:45.828
amount of space between you and

00:03:45.961 --> 00:03:47.263
the answer and let other people

00:03:47.396 --> 00:03:48.497
know, too, they are getting too

00:03:48.631 --> 00:03:48.797
close.

00:03:48.931 --> 00:03:51.166
You are not just putting

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:51.700
yourself in danger.

00:03:51.834 --> 00:03:52.434
You are putting other people in

00:03:52.568 --> 00:03:55.471
danger and putting the animals

00:03:55.604 --> 00:03:55.871
in danger.

00:03:56.005 --> 00:03:56.872
&gt;&gt; National parks are a

